  "description": "SUTRAC crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C56 H124 Ce6 N12 O24,2(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 5 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 5 O neighbors; Ce1B (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2B (Ce) has 5 O neighbors; Ce3B (Ce) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.601-3.662 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 105.86-108.57°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula Ce6O8(O2CtBu)8(L1)4·2CH3CN.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
